From ae88d46e53b9aa8c752f2a95abec074d8e6c6ac5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Caswell <matt@openssl.foundation>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:31:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ssl/quic/quic_impl.c: lock the QUIC connection in
 SSL_get_conn_close_info()
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ossl_quic_get_conn_close_info() reads the channel state and terminate
cause without taking the domain mutex. With thread assist, the assist
thread ticks the channel under that mutex and can change both at the
same time, so an application calling SSL_get_conn_close_info() from
another thread races with it.

The threads_sanitizer CI job hits this in quic_radix_test: after the
check_thread_assisted_idle script re-enables ticking on a
thread-assisted client, the harness calls SSL_get_conn_close_info()
on it from the main thread to print the final object state while the
assist thread is ticking. TSan reports a race in
ossl_quic_channel_is_term_any() only when the two overlap, so the job
fails intermittently.

Take the lock, as the other getters in quic_impl.c do.

Fixes: c3a04ea2fdd0 "QUIC DISPATCH/APL: Add SSL_stream_reset and status query APIs"
References: 3a9cedc20fe6 "QUIC APL: Rework QCTX to support listener calls"
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Reviewed-by: Tomas Mraz <tomas@openssl.foundation>
Reviewed-by: Nikola Pajkovsky <nikolap@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Saša Nedvědický <sashan@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Merge-date: Fri Nov  6 11:38:05 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33505
(cherry picked from commit 53990ac497823b22bff9a400714dc68cde77e0f6)
---
 ssl/quic/quic_impl.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ssl/quic/quic_impl.c b/ssl/quic/quic_impl.c
index a858a8c..92f85f0 100644
--- a/ssl/quic/quic_impl.c
+++ b/ssl/quic/quic_impl.c
@@ -4618,13 +4618,16 @@ int ossl_quic_get_conn_close_info(SSL *ssl,
 {
     QCTX ctx;
     const QUIC_TERMINATE_CAUSE *tc;
+    int ret = 0;
 
     if (!expect_quic_conn_only(ssl, &ctx))
         return -1;
 
+    qctx_lock(&ctx);
+
     tc = ossl_quic_channel_get_terminate_cause(ctx.qc->ch);
     if (tc == NULL)
-        return 0;
+        goto out;
 
     info->error_code = tc->error_code;
     info->frame_type = tc->frame_type;
@@ -4635,7 +4638,11 @@ int ossl_quic_get_conn_close_info(SSL *ssl,
         info->flags |= SSL_CONN_CLOSE_FLAG_LOCAL;
     if (!tc->app)
         info->flags |= SSL_CONN_CLOSE_FLAG_TRANSPORT;
-    return 1;
+    ret = 1;
+
+out:
+    qctx_unlock(&ctx);
+    return ret;
 }
 
